{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773527683,"nonce":"g84c899bg1YCNwpnawdsC3vc8oQ=","title":"Agent should rebase onto latest master before submitting for review","message":"## Problem\n\nWhen two nightshift sessions concurrently modify the same file, the second one to be accepted often has merge conflicts that require manual resolution.\n\nCurrent behavior: The agent completes its work, commits to the worktree branch, and submits for review without checking if master has moved since the branch was created.\n\nExpected behavior: Before marking work complete and submitting for review, the agent should:\n1. Fetch latest master\n2. Rebase the worktree branch onto master\n3. Re-run the full test suite to confirm no regressions\n4. Only then submit for review\n\nObserved in: leanaider project — issues a59f233 (null labels audit) and 8ff0088 (comment format fix) both modified gitbug.py. Accepting a59f233 first meant 8ff0088 conflicted on merge, requiring manual conflict resolution.\n\n## Implementation options\n\n### Option A: Add rebase step to WORKFLOW.md prompt\nAdd a rule to the prompt template telling the agent to rebase before @@DONE@@. Simplest, but relies on the agent following instructions — it may skip or fail silently.\n\n### Option B: Add pre-done hook in SessionRunner\nWhen the agent outputs @@DONE@@, before transitioning to waiting:review, run git fetch origin master \u0026\u0026 git rebase master in the worktree. If the rebase has conflicts, resume the agent with a prompt describing the conflicts. If tests fail after rebase, resume with that info.\n\n### Option C: Add rebase in host/launch.py post-container\nAfter the container exits with waiting:review, the host-side code rebases the branch onto master and re-runs tests. If conflicts arise, change status to working and re-launch.\n\nOption B seems best — it happens inside the container where the agent can fix conflicts itself.\n\n## Requirement\n\nREQ-006 (Merge and conflict handling)","files":null}]}